+\ POSTPONE) - there is no marker byte to scan back for. 0 when not found.
+VARIABLE T-XT
+VARIABLE T-THREAD
+: TNAME> ( t-nfa --- t-xt )  DUP C@-T 31 AND 1+ + ALIGNED-T ;
+: T-IMMEDIATE? ( t-xt --- flag )
+  T-XT !  T-THREAD @ CELLS TTHREADS + @
+  BEGIN DUP WHILE
+    DUP TNAME> T-XT @ = IF C@-T 64 AND EXIT THEN
+    TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ - DUP @-T DUP IF + ELSE SWAP DROP THEN
+  REPEAT ;
+
 : >BODY-T ( t-addr1 --- t-addr2 ) \ Convert executing token to param address.
   \ NOTE: this is target-address arithmetic and must use CELLS-T, not the
   \ host's CELLS. It only worked before because the host (RelF, 4-byte
@@ -437,7 +449,14 @@ FORWARD (POSTPONE)
 \ delimiters, so an empty string took the rest of the line (kernel.4's ABORT).
 : ." [ TRANSIENT ] (.") [ FORTH ] 34 PARSE DUP 1+ >R
       THERE PLACE-T R> ALLOT-T ALIGN-T ;
-: POSTPONE [ TRANSIENT ] (POSTPONE) [ FORTH ] T' THERE - ,-T ;
+\ Iteration 244: a target POSTPONE decides immediacy here, from the target
+\ header's IMMEDIATE bit - an immediate word compiled as a call (it runs when
+\ the definition runs), any other through (POSTPONE), which compiles it. The
+\ kernel's (POSTPONE) no longer asks >NAME at run time (a scan back for a
+\ marked byte, broken by UTF-8 names; bit 7 marks nothing now).
+: POSTPONE >IN @ BL WORD COUNT THASH T-THREAD ! >IN !
+  T' DUP T-IMMEDIATE? IF THERE - CELLBYTES-TOKEN - ,-T
+  ELSE [ TRANSIENT ] (POSTPONE) [ FORTH ] THERE - ,-T THEN ;
 : ABORT" [ TRANSIENT ] (ABORT") [ FORTH ] 34 PARSE DUP 1+ >R
       THERE PLACE-T R> ALLOT-T ALIGN-T ;
 
